course: dictionary
lesson: 2384
title: A name that became a unit
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and some names become words. «Marie Curie discovered two new elements, polonium and radium, separating tiny amounts of them from tonnes of ore.» Here Curie is a person's family name, so it starts with a capital letter.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like discovered, elements and radium tell you this is about science. Ask yourself: is this a person or a measurement? A curie is an old unit for measuring radioactivity, a bit like a metre or a gram measures something else.
explain: Marie Curie worked with her husband, Pierre. «Henri Becquerel discovered radioactivity in 1896; Marie Curie named it, studied it, and with Pierre Curie discovered polonium and radium.» Here the Curies are two people, so the capital letter is needed.
fact: Curie with a capital letter is a name, as in Marie Curie.
fact: Marie Curie was born in Poland, worked in France, and was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize.
fact: Marie Curie discovered the elements polonium and radium, and she studied radioactivity.
fact: She was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes, in two different sciences.
fact: A curie is an old unit for measuring radioactivity, and it is named after the Curies.
exercise: In «Marie Curie discovered two new elements», is Curie a name or a unit? | *A name of a person | A unit for measuring radioactivity | A chemical element | A type of rock
exercise: «A curie is an old unit for measuring radioactivity.» What is a curie used for? | Naming new countries | Cooking food | Winning prizes for science | *Measuring radioactivity
exercise: Marie Curie was born in Poland and worked in which other country? | Germany | Brazil | Spain | *France
test: What is a curie? | A type of bird | A kind of Nobel Prize | A French city | *An old unit for measuring radioactivity
test: Why does Curie have a capital letter in «with Pierre Curie discovered polonium»? | Because it is a unit | *Because it is the name of a person | Because it starts a sentence | Because it is very important
exam: Which statement is true? | She was born in France and worked in Poland | Curie is a type of bird | *She discovered polonium and radium | She discovered the element gold
